From b191bb893432c4df0551d24c85843d8513ed5a55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jnhu <me@hoooo.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:57:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] research(595-r5): rename the pass-fact signal to owner-pass
 activity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

R5 R4_CLEANUP item C2 (naming/comments/wrong-assertion fixes only; the
predicate and every runtime decision are unchanged). R4 finding C2: the
signal named pressure is not pending completion pressure — its
completed>0 disjunct counts work the observed owner pass already
published, and pressure_known meant "a pass was ever sampled", not
freshness. In the completion-driven W03 harness the predicate holds at
~99.92% of S decisions, including fully drained instants.

Renames (behavior identical, verified below):
- DecisionFacts::pressure_known -> owner_pass_sampled (monotonic
  liveness witness); its comment now states the lag and that
  last_pass_completed counts published work, not pending completions.
- BudgetVariant::read_pressure -> read_owner_pass_activity;
  Adapter::reads_pressure_facts -> reads_owner_pass_facts.
- budget::Input::{pressure_hint_active, pressure} ->
  {owner_pass_activity_hint_active, owner_pass_had_activity}; row
  "completion_pressure" -> "owner_pass_activity" (same predicate, same
  clamp2 effect, same table position).
- DecisionRecord::{pressure_read, pressure, pressure_known} ->
  {owner_pass_activity_read, owner_pass_had_activity,
  owner_pass_sampled}; the diag-line labels follow the field names.
- bench_w03_external_loop: SharedLoop::pressure_seen ->
  owner_pass_sampled; the publication-site comment now says the facts
  come from the final pass of the owner's drain loop and the flag is
  never cleared.
- r4_arm_smoke: assertions and labels that read the signal as a
  completion backlog ("completion backlog with active data",
  "pressured state") are corrected; the conditions keep testing the
  same values.

Deliberately unchanged: arm tokens SNI/SNP (frozen arm identities and
env interface), the r4_* record/counter schema including
r4_pressure_decisions (frozen R4 evidence statistic name and join key
to R4 RESULTS.md), and every predicate evaluation.

Validation (native E5, this session): 18-scenario ready-reuse oracle
(R4 archived source with only the renamed identifiers adapted; the
adaptation is recorded in r5 evidence), 18/18 rc=0, outputs identical
to baseline; r4_arm_smoke 57/57 checks PASS on both sides with only
the corrected labels differing; ready-batch deterministic/research/
fault oracles byte-identical; concurrency/cancel/shutdown suites rc=0;
W03 r3d16cap rc=0 for all arms.
